Flycast patches for dreamcast-sql (applied by build.sh to flyinghead/flycast 1b63c8a)

- reios/hostfs.cpp: a "BIOS" syscall at 0x8C00100A that gives the guest page I/O on
  $HOSTFS_PATH (+ -wal/-journal), two allow-listed env vars and the host clock.
- picoppp.cpp: FLYCAST_TCP_FORWARD / FLYCAST_TCP_BIND forward inbound host TCP ports to
  the emulated Broadband Adapter for any program, not just the games in its table; loopback
  clients appear to the guest as 198.18.0.1 (KallistiOS answers 127/8 on its own loopback);
  closed sockets are pruned from the acceptor; no public-IP / game-server DNS lookups.
- picotcp pico_socket_connect(): fail with EADDRINUSE when the socket's quad is already in
  the socket tree, instead of carrying on with an untracked socket whose later deletion
  unlinks and frees the other one (heap corruption). Linux reuses loopback source ports at
  once, so forwarded connections hit this; picoppp.cpp then lets picotcp pick a free port.
- picotcp heap.h: room for ~67,000 timers instead of ~1,000. Each TCP socket keeps several
  timers (keepalive, stats, retransmit, linger) and closed ones linger for 30 s, so a few dozen
  connections a second ran out; socket_del() then frees the socket at once while
  pico_tcp_input() is still using it (use-after-free, found with AddressSanitizer).

